// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE REQUEST SIDE OF THE CHAT COMPLETIONS CALL, AND THE PAYLOAD OF ONE STREAMED CHUNK.
//
// The section above models the answer of a non-streaming call. This models the other two shapes
// the same endpoint involves: what the caller sends, and what one event of a streamed answer
// carries. They sit together because one member of the request decides which answer shape
// arrives: `stream` false yields one OpenAiChatCompletion200Body, `stream` true yields a run of
// OpenAiChatCompletionChunkBody payloads, one JSON object per event. This module does not own the
// event framing -- extdeps.llm.openai_compat_sse owns the `data: ` line, the `[DONE]` sentinel,
// an error that arrives as a data line, and a stream that ends without the sentinel -- and it
// lists no products, engines or endpoints: the authority is the ExternalAuthority anchor at the
// top of this file, read 2026-11-01, whose member list is what the coverage rows below declare
// unmodelled rather than absent (DESIGN section 3, external upstream decomposition).
//
// WHY A SAMPLING PARAMETER IS CARRIED AS THE PARSER'S OWN JsonNumber, AND NEVER AS TEXT.
// std.float declares Float as a name with no operators and no ruled literal home -- its comment
// records that v2 refuses a float literal with infer_reason_float_literal_home_unruled -- and the
// json parser keeps a number as JsonNumber { lexeme } without ever evaluating it. So a request
// read that produced a Float for `temperature` would be inventing a numeric home the language has
// not ruled, and a caller that compared `temperature` as TEXT would be validating a string
// standing in for a number. The carrier is therefore the parser's own JsonNumber: a typed JSON
// number lexeme with its standing, no range check, no comparison, and nothing here re-encodes a
// body -- a forwarder that re-emits the lexeme it read sends the client's bytes back out
// unchanged. openai_chat_completion_wire_frontier_rows names the one trigger that turns these
// into values: a ruled Float literal and operator home in std.float.
type OpenAiCompletionStop
  = StopAtString { text: String }
  | StopAtStrings { texts: List<String> }

type OpenAiStreamOptions {
  include_usage: Bool
}

// `max_tokens` is the member the anchor documents for this endpoint. The Responses API's
// `max_output_tokens` is a different endpoint's member and is not borrowed in here.
type OpenAiChatCompletionRequest {
  model: String
  messages: List<OpenAiChatMessage>
  max_tokens: Int?
  n: Int?
  seed: Int?
  stop: OpenAiCompletionStop?
  stream: Bool
  stream_options: OpenAiStreamOptions?
  reasoning_effort: OpenAiReasoningEffort?
  temperature: JsonNumber?
  top_p: JsonNumber?
  presence_penalty: JsonNumber?
  frequency_penalty: JsonNumber?
}

// WHY THIS IS THE SIXTH COPY OF A PAIR AND IS NOT YET GENERALIZED (§6b). Five members of this file
// already carry the same construction -- a wire-name table, a chain that reads it, an arm that keeps
// an unknown name whole, and a match that re-emits (OpenAiToolCallType, OpenAiResponsesOutputContentType,
// OpenAiResponsesOutputItemType, OpenAiResponsesStatus, OpenAiResponsesOutputItemStatus). §6b rejects a
// repeated pattern until the author answers why it should not be generalized. The answer here is: it
// SHOULD be, and not now, for two reasons that are facts rather than convenience. (1) Generalizing means
// rewriting five members this PR does not own, three of them the Responses API shapes, and changing what
// a parse returns for an undocumented wire name is a behavioural change on readers this PR has not read;
// the honest unit of that change is one PR per upstream surface, with its readers. (2) The generic shape
// is not yet determined by evidence: the six copies differ in whether an unknown name is kept, refused,
// or folded into a status, and a table written now would be guessed rather than read off the last copy.
// The follow-up is declared, not assumed: openai_chat_completion_wire_frontier_rows carries the row, whose
// trigger is the seventh member or the first migration, and whose carrier is a wire-name table over a type
// parameter (the language has parametric declarations: std.algebra Magma<T>, std.affine_space
// SpatialResult<T>) with the unknown-name and empty-name arms supplied per member.
//
// An enumerated member: wire name in, variant out. A request that names a fifth effort is not
// silently read as one of the four, and it is not refused here either -- the endpoint owns the
// answer to an effort it does not know; this model only reports the shape.
//
// THE EMPTY NAME IS REFUSED, NOT CARRIED. `raw` is a `NonEmptyStr`, which is
// `String where string_non_empty`, and that predicate is enforced at LITERAL sites only until
// compile-time evaluation lands (std.types, feature:where-refinement-predicate-declaration-authority).
// So routing an empty name into that field would put an empty string behind a type whose name
// promises otherwise, and nothing would say so -- the type would be doing the lying. The refusal is
// its own arm rather than a Bool parameter or a sanitizing default, because an absent name and an
// undocumented name are three different facts the caller may need to tell apart, and §5 refuses
// silently widening a failure arm. This is a fact about THIS endpoint's wire, not a general string
// law; the general law, if one is ever needed, is std.types' predicate and stays there.
type OpenAiReasoningEffort
  = EffortMinimal
  | EffortLow
  | EffortMedium
  | EffortHigh
  | UndocumentedEffortName { raw: NonEmptyStr }
  | EmptyEffortName

data openai_reasoning_effort_minimal_wire: String = "minimal"
data openai_reasoning_effort_low_wire: String = "low"
data openai_reasoning_effort_medium_wire: String = "medium"
data openai_reasoning_effort_high_wire: String = "high"

fn parse_openai_reasoning_effort(raw: String) -> OpenAiReasoningEffort {
  if raw == openai_reasoning_effort_minimal_wire { EffortMinimal }
  else if raw == openai_reasoning_effort_low_wire { EffortLow }
  else if raw == openai_reasoning_effort_medium_wire { EffortMedium }
  else if raw == openai_reasoning_effort_high_wire { EffortHigh }
  else if raw == "" { EmptyEffortName }
  else { UndocumentedEffortName { raw: raw } }
}

fn openai_reasoning_effort_wire(effort: OpenAiReasoningEffort) -> String {
  match effort {
    EffortMinimal => openai_reasoning_effort_minimal_wire
    EffortLow => openai_reasoning_effort_low_wire
    EffortMedium => openai_reasoning_effort_medium_wire
    EffortHigh => openai_reasoning_effort_high_wire
    UndocumentedEffortName { raw: r } => r
    EmptyEffortName => ""
  }
}

// ONE EVENT PAYLOAD of a streamed answer. The delta is what changed since the previous event: the
// first event usually carries a role and no content, a middle event carries content and no role,
// the last carries a finish_reason and neither. So every delta member is optional, and absent is
// not empty -- an empty `content` is a token that is the empty string, which is a different fact
// from a chunk that sent no content member at all.
data openai_chat_completion_chunk_object_wire: String = "chat.completion.chunk"

type OpenAiChatCompletionChunkDelta {
  role: OpenAiChatMessageRole?
  content: String?
  refusal: String?
}

type OpenAiChatCompletionChunkChoice {
  index: Int
  delta: OpenAiChatCompletionChunkDelta
  logprobs: OpenAiChatCompletion200Logprobs?
  finish_reason: OpenAiFinishReason?
}

type OpenAiChatCompletionChunkBody {
  id: String
  object: String
  created: Int
  model: String
  choices: List<OpenAiChatCompletionChunkChoice>
  usage: OpenAiChatCompletion200Usage?
  service_tier: String?
  system_fingerprint: String?
}

// A streamed chunk's tool-call deltas are PARTIAL: an event may carry only a call index and a
// fragment of one argument string, with no id and no function name, so the ToolCall record above
// (id, type, function) cannot hold one. Modelling the accumulation is its own change: it needs a
// decision about where the partial call is held between events, which belongs with whoever reads
// the stream, not with the wire shape. Declared here rather than papered over with optional
// fields on ToolCall, which would let a non-streaming request carry a half call.
data structural_coverage_gap_openai_chat_chunk_tool_call_deltas: List<CoverageClosureEntry> = [
  {
    facts: [
      Subject { path: "OpenAiChatCompletionChunkDelta" },
      Missing { item: "tool_call_delta_with_index_and_argument_fragment" },
      Missing { item: "function_call_delta" }
    ],
    trigger: "a named home for a partial tool call held across events, with its accumulation rule"
  }
]

// The request members this model does not carry, from the same anchor. Each is a member a caller
// may send today; a caller that sends one is not thereby malformed. They are declared missing
// rather than omitted, so the next change that needs one extends this record instead of
// re-reading the endpoint's shape somewhere else.
data structural_coverage_gap_openai_chat_completion_request_members: List<CoverageClosureEntry> = [
  {
    facts: [
      Subject { path: "OpenAiChatCompletionRequest" },
      Missing { item: "logit_bias" },
      Missing { item: "logprobs_and_top_logprobs" },
      Missing { item: "response_format" },
      Missing { item: "tools_tool_choice_parallel_tool_calls" },
      Missing { item: "legacy_functions_and_function_call" },
      Missing { item: "audio" },
      Missing { item: "modalities" },
      Missing { item: "prediction" },
      Missing { item: "max_completion_tokens" },
      Missing { item: "service_tier" },
      Missing { item: "store_and_metadata" },
      Missing { item: "safety_identifier_and_user" },
      Missing { item: "web_search_options" },
      Missing { item: "prompt_cache_key" }
    ],
    trigger: "the first member a serving call must read or forward beyond sampling -- tools and response_format before the rest"
  }
]

// A sampling parameter is carried as an un-evaluated JSON number lexeme. That is a frontier, not
// a design: it dissolves when the language rules a float literal and operator home, at which
// point these four fields become numbers and any read that compares them becomes meaningful.
data openai_chat_completion_wire_frontier_rows: List<FrontierRow> = [
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.llm.openai", decl_name: "OpenAiChatCompletionRequest"),
    reason: "temperature, top_p, presence_penalty and frequency_penalty are carried as the json parser's JsonNumber lexeme, because std.float declares Float as a name with no operators and no ruled literal home (v2 refuses a float literal: infer_reason_float_literal_home_unruled), and the json parser never evaluates a number's lexeme. Nothing here range-checks or orders them: that would be validation on text standing in for a number",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "feature:std-float-literal-and-operator-home - std.float rules a float literal home and the comparison operators for it, and extdeps.languages.json reads a lexeme into that value; then these four members are typed as that value, a read that rejects an out-of-range sampling parameter becomes meaningful and is placed at the caller that owns the range, and this row deletes. The lexeme path stays for a forwarder that must re-emit the client's bytes unchanged"),
  ),
  // The request record has no reader yet. Its consumer is named rather than assumed: the request
  // read of the serving path, which the approved plan dag/gunbc/plans/fabric_serving_router.dag
  // puts in its S3 decisions (model, stream, stop and reasoning_effort are exactly what that read
  // needs), and the dashboard client that sends the call. The row exists so an unread model is
  // tracked as debt (DESIGN section 3c) instead of being deleted quietly when the read lands.
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.llm.openai", decl_name: "OpenAiChatCompletionRequest"),
    reason: "no module reads this record yet: the only consumer today is its own witness, and a model nobody reads is not yet evidence that the shape is right",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "feature:s3-serving-request-read - the serving path's request read, which the approved plan gunbc.plans.fabric_serving_router puts in its S3 decisions, reads model, stream, stop and reasoning_effort out of this record, and the dashboard client builds it for the call it sends. It dissolves when that reader lands WITH a witness that builds a request of this shape and reads it back, so the record is paid for by an observation and not by a compile. The read belongs to that plan, not to this module: nothing here decides what to do with a request"),
  ),
  // The repeated enumerated-member pair, declared as debt with its carrier named rather than left
  // in a comment: §6b allows deferring a generalization only with a stated reason and trigger.
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.llm.openai", decl_name: "OpenAiReasoningEffort"),
    reason: "the wire-name pair (table, read chain, unknown-keeping arm, re-emitting match) is written out by hand for the sixth time in this module; DESIGN section 6b makes the second local implementation the trigger to generalize, and the reason it is deferred here is in the comment above OpenAiReasoningEffort: rewriting five members this change does not own -- three of them Responses API shapes -- would change what an undocumented wire name reads to for readers this change has not read",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "feature:openai-wire-name-table-generalization - the seventh enumerated member of this module, or the first migration of an existing five, whichever comes first: one wire-name table over a type parameter (parametric declarations exist: std.algebra Magma<T>, std.affine_space SpatialResult<T>) taking the member's rows plus the unknown-name and empty-name arms, so adding a variant means adding a row and the pair is written once. The migrating PR must carry the readers of each member it converts, member by member"),
  ),
  // Same for the streamed payload: the framing is already read by extdeps.llm.openai_compat_sse,
  // but nothing yet reads what one of those events carries.
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.llm.openai", decl_name: "OpenAiChatCompletionChunkBody"),
    reason: "no module reads one chunk payload yet; openai_compat_sse frames the events and this record describes their content, and the two are only joined by a reader",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "feature:s3-streamed-answer-read - the serving path's streamed read named in the approved plan gunbc.plans.fabric_serving_router's S3 decisions forwards one payload of this shape and closes the usage record at stream end. It dissolves when that reader lands WITH a witness that decodes a recorded chat.completion.chunk -- the role-only first event, a content delta, and the finish_reason-only last event -- into this record"),
  ),
]

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE LEGACY TEXT COMPLETIONS ENDPOINT, /v1/completions. The chat endpoint above is the one most
// callers reach for; this one is served alongside it by the engines the rented cards run, and the
// model is not "chat minus messages" -- the prompt is a union of four shapes, three members exist
// only here (suffix, echo, best_of), and a choice carries a string where a chat choice carries a
// message or a delta. Its authority is its own anchor below: the two endpoints are documented and
// versioned separately, and borrowing the chat anchor would let a change to one silently claim
// authority over the other. Read 2026-11-01.
data extdeps_completions_external_authority_anchor: ExternalAuthority = ExternalAuthority {
  uri: Uri {
    scheme: Https
    locator: "platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/completions/create"
  }
}

// Both this endpoint's answer shapes name themselves with this literal, streamed and not, and it is
// NOT the chat chunk's literal: a reader that branches on `object` must not be able to confuse a
// whole text-completion answer with one event of a streamed chat answer.
data openai_text_completion_object_wire: String = "text_completion"

// THE `object` MEMBER IS A CONSTANT IN THE SPEC, SO IT IS TYPED AS ONE, NOT AS A FREE STRING: the
// value is the wire constant above, and the constraint is this module's where-predicate. std.types
// spells NonEmptyStr exactly this way (`type NonEmptyStr = String where string_non_empty`, with the
// predicate as an ordinary fn beside it at std/types.dag:264-277), so the where atom binds to a
// declaration in the same module. It lives here rather than as a bare `String` because the two
// endpoints' bodies are otherwise indistinguishable at the type: a `chat.completion`, a
// `chat.completion.chunk` and an error envelope would each type-check as a text completion, which is
// the confusion the constant exists to prevent. A reader decoding a response must therefore REFUSE
// when `object` is not this constant, and that refusal is the consumer this constant exists for --
// its executing route is //test/claim/extdeps/openai_text_completion_wire_witness, which calls the
// predicate with the documented value and with each chat endpoint's value, so a constant that drifted
// goes red. Where-refinements are enforced at literal sites today, so the decoder is where the
// constraint bites in practice; declaring it is the model fact, exactly as NonEmptyStr is.
fn openai_text_completion_object_is_documented(value: String) -> Bool {
  value == openai_text_completion_object_wire
}

type OpenAiTextCompletionObject = String where openai_text_completion_object_is_documented

// The prompt member as the endpoint document gives it. Four arms, each cited to the one member's union
// in the anchor above (platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/completions/create, member
// `completions-prompt`, read 2026-11-01), which lists exactly these four shapes and no others:
//   PromptText       -- string             one prompt, one completion
//   PromptTexts      -- array<string>      one completion per entry
//   PromptTokens     -- array<int>         one prompt, already tokenized by the caller
//   PromptTokenLists -- array<array<int>>  several tokenized prompts
// A coproduct rather than a String field, because a String folds the four together and loses the
// difference between one prompt containing a comma and two prompts -- which is the difference between
// one completion and two, so it is not a detail a reader can recover. Tokens stay integers here: they
// are already the engine's own vocabulary, and re-rendering them as text would make the tokenizer's
// decision a routing fact.
type OpenAiCompletionPrompt
  = PromptText { text: String }
  | PromptTexts { texts: List<String> }
  | PromptTokens { tokens: List<Int> }
  | PromptTokenLists { token_lists: List<List<Int>> }

// The sampling members are the same carrier as the chat request's, for the same reason: std.float has
// no ruled literal or operator home, the json parser keeps a number as an un-evaluated lexeme, and
// nothing here compares or range-checks them. `openai_chat_completion_wire_frontier_rows` carries that
// frontier for both endpoints' requests; a ruled float home dissolves one, not one per endpoint.
type OpenAiTextCompletionRequest {
  model: String
  prompt: OpenAiCompletionPrompt?
  suffix: String?
  max_tokens: Int?
  best_of: Int?
  echo: Bool?
  n: Int?
  seed: Int?
  stop: OpenAiCompletionStop?
  stream: Bool
  stream_options: OpenAiStreamOptions?
  temperature: JsonNumber?
  top_p: JsonNumber?
  presence_penalty: JsonNumber?
  frequency_penalty: JsonNumber?
}

type OpenAiTextCompletionChoice {
  index: Int
  text: String
  finish_reason: OpenAiFinishReason?
}

// `usage` is the chat record, reused. The two endpoint documents give that member the same shape and
// the same members, so a second record with the same fields would put one fact in two places and let
// them drift while both claimed to describe usage. `choices` is deliberately NOT shared: here a choice
// is a string, there it is a message.
type OpenAiTextCompletion200Body {
  id: String
  object: OpenAiTextCompletionObject
  created: Int
  model: String
  choices: List<OpenAiTextCompletionChoice>
  usage: OpenAiChatCompletion200Usage?
  service_tier: String?
  system_fingerprint: String?
}

// One event of a streamed answer from this endpoint. Two facts a reader needs and cannot infer from
// the non-streaming shape: the final event carries a finish_reason and NO text, so `text` is optional
// here while it is required above; and an engine may send a closing frame with usage and an empty
// choices list, so `choices` is a list that may be empty rather than a non-empty one.
type OpenAiTextCompletionChunkChoice {
  index: Int
  text: String?
  finish_reason: OpenAiFinishReason?
}

type OpenAiTextCompletionChunkBody {
  id: String
  object: OpenAiTextCompletionObject
  created: Int
  model: String
  choices: List<OpenAiTextCompletionChunkChoice>
  usage: OpenAiChatCompletion200Usage?
}

data structural_coverage_gap_openai_text_completion_members: List<CoverageClosureEntry> = [
  {
    facts: [
      Subject { path: "OpenAiTextCompletionRequest" },
      Missing { item: "logit_bias" },
      Missing { item: "logprobs" },
      Missing { item: "user" }
    ],
    trigger: "the first member a serving call must forward on this endpoint beyond sampling -- logprobs before the rest, since it is the one that cannot be recovered after the answer arrives"
  },
  {
    facts: [
      Subject { path: "OpenAiTextCompletionChoice" },
      Missing { item: "logprobs_token_ranks" }
    ],
    trigger: "a reader that prices or explains a completion by token rank; the chat side's OpenAiChatCompletion200Logprobs is the shape to compare against before inventing a second one"
  },
  {
    facts: [
      Subject { path: "OpenAiTextCompletionChunkChoice" },
      Missing { item: "logprobs_token_ranks" }
    ],
    trigger: "the streamed counterpart of the row above, which needs the accumulation rule for per-token logprobs across events"
  }
]

// No module reads the text-completion shapes yet, and the consumer is named rather than assumed: the
// same serving-path read that the approved plan gunbc.plans.fabric_serving_router puts in its S3
// decisions, on whichever endpoint the client called. Tracked as debt (DESIGN section 3c) so an unread
// model cannot be deleted quietly, and so its absence is visible rather than implied by the endpoint
// existing.
data openai_text_completion_wire_frontier_rows: List<FrontierRow> = [
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.llm.openai", decl_name: "OpenAiTextCompletionRequest"),
    reason: "no module builds or reads this record yet: its only consumer is the naming of it in this module's own coverage rows",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "feature:s3-completions-request-read - the serving path's request read in the approved plan gunbc.plans.fabric_serving_router's S3 decisions, on the /v1/completions endpoint: it reads this record's model, stream, prompt shape and stop, and a client builds the record for the call it sends. It dissolves when that reader lands WITH a witness that builds a request of this shape and reads it back. The decisions about a request belong to that plan, not here"),
  ),
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.llm.openai", decl_name: "OpenAiTextCompletion200Body"),
    reason: "no module reads a non-streaming text-completion answer yet, and none refuses a body whose `object` member is not the documented constant",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "feature:s3-completions-answer-read - the serving path's read in the approved plan gunbc.plans.fabric_serving_router's S3 decisions closes a usage record from one body of this shape. It dissolves when that reader lands WITH a witness that decodes a recorded completions 200 body into this record and asserts its choices and usage, so a shape nobody has fed real bytes through is not carried as truth"),
  ),
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.llm.openai", decl_name: "OpenAiTextCompletionChunkBody"),
    reason: "no module reads one streamed text-completion event yet, and none refuses a payload whose `object` member is not the documented constant; openai_compat_sse frames such events but does not interpret their content",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "feature:s3-completions-chunk-read - the serving path's streamed read in the approved plan gunbc.plans.fabric_serving_router's S3 decisions forwards one payload of this shape and finishes the answer at the sentinel. It dissolves when that reader lands WITH a witness that decodes a recorded completions chunk into this record -- including the final event, which carries a finish_reason and no text"),
  ),
]
